<!--
    Arabic, and the reason it is a whole file rather than a nice-to-have.

    This product ships in the UAE. The *server* has been bilingual since the
    subject seam was written — every provider carries LabelAr, every action
    carries a label_ar, and the price line, badge and CTA on a reel already
    arrive translated because the client sends Accept-Language. So the content
    was Arabic and the chrome around it was English, which is the worst of both:
    a screen where the car is described in Arabic and the button under it says
    "Message seller".

    Two things are worth knowing about the translations here.

    **Numbers stay Western.** Arabic-Indic digits (٠١٢٣) are correct in a great
    deal of Arabic typesetting and wrong for this: prices, mileages and phone
    numbers in the Gulf are written in Western digits almost universally, and a
    price rendered ١٨٩٬٠٠٠ next to a listing card showing 189,000 reads as two
    different cars. The format arguments pass through unchanged.

    **Layout direction is Android's problem, not this file's.** The manifest
    already declares supportsRtl, and every screen in the app uses `start`/`end`
    padding rather than `left`/`right`, so mirroring is automatic. The one place
    it is not is a hard-coded glyph: "‹" for back becomes wrong in RTL, and
    Compose does not mirror a text character. Left as-is and noted, because the
    fix is an icon rather than a string.
-->
